{
  "id": "building.research-lab",
  "version": "v1",
  "kind": "enterable-building",
  "space": "building-local — origin at footprint ground-centre, floor plane y=0, +Y up, entrance faces +Z, breach flank +X. AABBs are min/max in world units (u).",
  "units": {
    "sourceUnit": "powerworld-world-unit",
    "symbol": "u",
    "metersPerUnit": 0.1875,
    "gameConversion": "1:1 — the recipe is authored directly in PowerWorld world units, so no scale is applied at import. The metre figure is documentation only.",
    "derivation": "Measured from the runtime, not guessed: src/engine/citytiles.js door metric `DH = 11.2 * M` is commented 'a 2.1m doorway', so 2.1 m / 11.2 u = 0.1875 m/u; the same file builds a 9.6u human = 1.8 m. 1 m = 5.3333 u."
  },
  "axes": {
    "up": "+Y",
    "front": "+Z",
    "rightFlank": "+X",
    "handedness": "right-handed (glTF 2.0)",
    "note": "Building origin (0,0,0) is the ground-centre of the footprint, floor plane at y=0. The entrance faces +Z; the breach panel is on the +X flank. The runtime places the building by an (x,z) world centre and a yaw; these local axes rotate with that yaw."
  },
  "note": "Stable-ID collider pieces. `collider` = blocks movement/projectiles; `standable` = you can rest on its top (role floor/step/roof/prop); `breakable` pieces vanish when their breakGroup breaks (state \"intact-only\"). Decor pieces (collider:false, standable:false) are render-only and carry no physics. This is the AUTHORITATIVE physics description; the GLB nodes (same `node` names) are render only.",
